{"id":172654834944235,"type":"album","name":"Solo Monk","artist":"Thelonious Monk","year":1965,"weight":11,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710309.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-21b363b7-e40e-4f8c-a6e3-613a06226fa0/mbid-21b363b7-e40e-4f8c-a6e3-613a06226fa0-21120304379.jpg","yt":"i61gSKmeQ74","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/thelonious-monk/solo-monk"},"desc":"The mystery and haunting angular beauty of Thelonious Monk's unadorned keyboard sides are the focus of Solo Monk. As if possessing the history of jazz in his hands, Monk's solo recordings and performances from every phase of his career remain pure. The components of what made Monk such an uncompromising composer, arranger, and especially bandmember are evident in every note he plays. The disc includes both Monk originals as well as several covers of pop music standards. A majority of these sides were cut during a West Coast swing in late-October/early-November 1964. This highly productive jaunt would likewise yield two ."},"artist_ref":{"id":220093338227197,"name":"Thelonious Monk","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Thelonious_Monk%2C_Minton%27s_Playhouse%2C_New_York%2C_N.Y.%2C_ca._Sept._1947_%28William_P._Gottlieb_06191%29.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":265524373450282,"type":"genre","name":"jazz","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1461,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":261516756034660,"type":"genre","name":"Ragtime","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":247,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":33310639067833,"type":"genre","name":"Northern American Music","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":200,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":173049125996624,"type":"genre","name":"Stride","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":140,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":265238898886802,"name":"RYM Top — Jazz — Stride","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":1,"year":null,"note":null,"total":142,"scaruffi":null},{"id":280702155250789,"name":"RYM Top — Reg